{"authored" [{"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6t+2.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=2.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=2.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(6t+2)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(3{t}^{2}+2t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[3(2)^{2}+2(2)]-[3(1)^{2}+2(1)] \\\\  & =[12+4]-[3+2] \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =(5-1)^{3/2}-(1-1)^{3/2} \\\\  & =8-0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ the particle is located at the position $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{2}+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{6}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3+{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =3+([\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]-[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]) \\\\  & =3+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =3+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "902c39eabe7fa5fcd71f6ab8a5ed2992b55ce2683462c85bb8214aade1abfe5e" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2t+3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{2}+{t}^{3})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}+{3}^{3}]-[{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =[9+27]-[1+1] \\\\  & =36-2 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "902c39eabe7fa5fcd71f6ab8a5ed2992b55ce2683462c85bb8214aade1abfe5e" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t.$ At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf39f066a9bebfa423e36e53e5d26410735ad5e78e6a00d4cf8f063443a3f4c3" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =-20+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-20+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-20+([2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]-[2(2)^{3}+2(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-20+([128+32]-[16+8]) \\\\  & =-20+(160-24) \\\\  & =-20+136 \\\\  & =116.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf39f066a9bebfa423e36e53e5d26410735ad5e78e6a00d4cf8f063443a3f4c3" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "d2c6d2782d678e247239b6b0463883ecc5c6091a11425d6c62613dbf202fecf5" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "d2c6d2782d678e247239b6b0463883ecc5c6091a11425d6c62613dbf202fecf5" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-2413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=8{t}^{2}-3t.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=0$ and $t=6?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}(8{t}^{2}-3t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{8{t}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{8(6)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3(6)^{2}}{2}]-[\\frac{8(0)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3(0)^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =[576-54]-0 \\\\  & =522.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=6$ is $522.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-2413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "494"] ["math" "505"] ["math" "522"] ["math" "614"] ["math" "723"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "522"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =(5-1)^{3/2}-(1-1)^{3/2} \\\\  & =8-0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6t+2.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=2.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=2.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(6t+2)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(3{t}^{2}+2t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[3(2)^{2}+2(2)]-[3(1)^{2}+2(1)] \\\\  & =[12+4]-[3+2] \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-84263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=4\\sqrt[3]{t}-1.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=8?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-84263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{8}(4\\sqrt[3]{t}-1)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3{t}^{4/3}-t){|}_{1}^{8} \\\\  & =[3(8)^{4/3}-8]-[3(1)^{4/3}-1] \\\\  & =[48-8]-[3-1] \\\\  & =40-2 \\\\  & =38.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=8$ is $38.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-84263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-84263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-84263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "37"] ["math" "38"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "43"] ["math" "54"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-84263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "38"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}-2t.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[2(4)^{3}-(4)^{2}]-[2(1)^{3}-(1)^{2}] \\\\  & =[128-16]-[2-1] \\\\  & =112-1 \\\\  & =111.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=4$ is $111.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "111"] ["math" "148"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "88"] ["math" "92"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "111"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)={sec}^{2}⁡(t).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-2+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2+{[\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =-2+1-0 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is $x=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-351445" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351445" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-348283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ the particle is located at the position $x=1.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi .$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-348283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =1+{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =1+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =1+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]) \\\\  & =1+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =1+(-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+1) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+1 \\\\  & =2+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=2+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-348283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-348283" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-348283" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{6}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3+{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =3+([\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]-[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]) \\\\  & =3+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =3+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ the particle is located at the position $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{2}+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)={2}^{2t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=-5.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=3$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,3].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(3)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(3) & =-5+{\\int }_{1}^{3}({2}^{2t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-5+{[{2}^{2t-2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-5+{2}^{2(3)-2}-{2}^{2(1)-2} \\\\  & =-5+{2}^{4}-{2}^{0} \\\\  & =-5+16-1 \\\\  & =-5+15 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351463" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/1df00f421b20b101d1500b4e2f47054f0c79dcfd2d82585fb8fb3735adb71af5.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=5.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=9?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=9$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,9].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(9)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=5,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=9.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(9)=5+2=7.\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=9$ is $x=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/cb931a29b19302801d6586c37b4d2282e37776aa58b761f1fcb088a8fa19f9ff.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=1,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=1+4=5.\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-121014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-49319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/aad42b26d165789da802c0f507e3445976f3269b4c77e8b47201fb043b08f1f6.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=6.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-49319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=3$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,3].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(3)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=6$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=3.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(3)=6+5=11\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-49319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-49319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-49319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-49319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/18904539463b95f9d681f61f0d8f875ad0cb03b35d4037e75c227d4523502193.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(1)=2,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=1$ to $t=5.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(5)=2+6=8.\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/981252abc3668e62a5c9289c918d1231ec9a83745f70a00f0da4c85f194b8215.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=4,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=4$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [4,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(4)=-3$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=4$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=-3+3=0.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b"} {"question" "q-351501" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "q-351501" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad7041e4f5a2d244d1bacc0db583be37ec458c8abe9f903261b3eaaa01672e9d"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "b8898e26a80178eac6b570ed5da3c8ff2273acceb8265730797b7a0cb2b7f102"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2t+3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{2}+{t}^{3})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}+{3}^{3}]-[{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =[9+27]-[1+1] \\\\  & =36-2 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "b8898e26a80178eac6b570ed5da3c8ff2273acceb8265730797b7a0cb2b7f102"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t.$ At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf5431d28318289d2b378f362fd185a578fd2d6248ac545fb395229c648236eb"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =-20+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-20+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-20+([2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]-[2(2)^{3}+2(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-20+([128+32]-[16+8]) \\\\  & =-20+(160-24) \\\\  & =-20+136 \\\\  & =116.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf5431d28318289d2b378f362fd185a578fd2d6248ac545fb395229c648236eb"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "863e847ff57a5694a6c8facc39dacc346c93ec5ce1d87b780d9cc602d90aaaa5"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "863e847ff57a5694a6c8facc39dacc346c93ec5ce1d87b780d9cc602d90aaaa5"}] "usage" {"q-121007" [] "q-351431" [] "e-568" [] "q-49319" [] "e-7128" [] "e-7129" [] "q-2409" [] "q-81506" [] "q-351421" []} "basis" 1524 "retractions" [[17592186176357 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^{2} - 2t$. What is the total displacement of the particle between $t = 1$ and $t = 4$?"] [17592186176420 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3576/Source/Images/q-49319.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t = 0$ the particle is located at the positi